Affect         -1 -1 8 13 0
Affect         -1 -1 5 1 0
#EXDESC
ExDescKey  gauntlets sith alchemical dark~
ExDesc     Gauntlets worked with Sith alchemy, their metal fused with
dark side energy at the molecular level by a process no longer
understood. The fingers end in reinforced tips that can punch
through light armour. The dark side enhancement to combat
capability they provide is measurable and substantial.
~
#ENDEXDESC
#ENDOBJECT

#OBJECT
Vnum       33005
Keywords   sith tome tome ancient dark knowledge~
Short      an ancient Sith tome~
Long       An ancient Sith tome lies open here, its pages covered in dark script.~
Type       armor~
Flags      magic~
WFlags     take hold~
Values     12 12 0 0 0 0
Stats      10 18000 1800 0 0
Affect         -1 -1 10 3 0
Affect         -1 -1 8 4 0
#EXDESC
ExDescKey  tome sith ancient dark knowledge~
ExDesc     A Sith tome from the height of the old Empire, its pages made
from a material that has survived millennia without deterioration.
The knowledge within covers dark side techniques, Sith alchemy,
and the theory of power in a depth that is genuinely dangerous.
Reading it improves certain capabilities substantially and
makes sleep considerably more difficult.
~
#ENDEXDESC
#ENDOBJECT

#OBJECT
Vnum       33006
Keywords   sith helm mask dark lord ancient~
Short      a Sith Lord's battle helm~
Long       A Sith Lord's battle helm rests here, its visor dark as the void.~
Type       armor~
Flags      magic~
WFlags     take head~
Values     60 60 0 0 0 0
Stats      10 24000 2400 0 0
Affect         -1 -1 -25 12 0
Affect         -1 -1 8 13 0
Affect         -1 -1 6 5 0
#EXDESC
ExDescKey  helm mask sith lord battle dark~
ExDesc     The battle helm of a Sith Lord, its faceplate fashioned into an
expression of absolute authority. The visor enhances vision across
all spectra and a voice modulator built into the vocaliser gives
the wearer's speech a resonance that is not entirely natural in
origin. Donning it creates an immediate and not unpleasant sense
of dominance.
~
#ENDEXDESC
#ENDOBJECT

#OBJECT
Vnum       33007
Keywords   sith ring dark power bone~
Short      a Sith bone ring~
Long       A ring carved from bone and set with a dark crystal lies here.~
Type       armor~
Flags      magic glow~
WFlags     take finger~
Values     8 8 0 0 0 0
Stats      10 15000 1500 0 0
Affect         -1 -1 5 3 0
Affect         -1 -1 5 4 0
Affect         -1 -1 5 14 0
#EXDESC
ExDescKey  ring sith bone dark crystal power~
ExDesc     A ring carved from bone — not animal bone — set with a faceted
dark crystal that absorbs light rather than reflecting it. The dark
side energy in the crystal enhances mental focus and power of will
in ways that are difficult to describe and easy to become dependent
on. It fits perfectly regardless of finger size.
~
#ENDEXDESC
#ENDOBJECT

#ROOM
Vnum     33000
Name     Korriban Spaceport — Landing Platform~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors can_land~
Desc     The landing platform of Korriban's single functional spaceport is bare
durasteel swept by a constant hot wind carrying red dust from the
valley beyond. The port operates with minimal staff — few ships come
to Korriban willingly and the ones that do are not interested in
customer service. The air tastes of iron and something older. The
spaceport terminal lies to the north and the road toward the valley
begins to the east.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33001
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33002
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 1 33000
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33001
Name     Korriban Spaceport — Terminal~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The spaceport terminal is a study in deliberate intimidation. Dark stone
walls, minimal lighting, and the symbol of the Sith Empire carved above
every doorway make the message clear: this is not a welcoming place.
A single customs station processes arrivals with the thoroughness of
those who expect to find contraband because they usually do. The landing
platform lies to the south and the main exit leads east toward the town.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33000
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33003
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 1 33001
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33002
Name     The Spaceport Road~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A road of dark compacted stone leads east from the spaceport toward
the valley settlements. Red dust drifts across the road in the hot
wind and the sky above is a deep burnt orange. In the distance the
silhouette of the Sith Academy is visible against the cliffs. The
landscape is harsh and stripped of all softness — Korriban offers
nothing that is not earned.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33000
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33004
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 2 33002
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33003
Name     Dreshdae Settlement — Main Street~
Sector   city~
Flags    ~
Desc     Dreshdae is the only settlement on Korriban worth the name, a collection
of utilitarian structures built for function and nothing else. The main
street runs between supply depots, a cantina, and the various operations
that support the Academy above. The inhabitants are Sith acolytes on
leave, merchants with no choice but to be here, and the occasional
traveller who has made a significant navigational error. The spaceport
is to the west and the valley road begins to the north.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33001
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33005
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33006
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33007
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 3 33003
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33004
Name     The Wasteland Road~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The road from the spaceport meets the main valley road here in a wide
junction marked by a carved stone pillar bearing Sith script. The
translation is approximately: strength through victory, victory through
power. The surrounding landscape is red rock and dust as far as the
horizon in every direction. Nothing grows here. Nothing has grown
here for a very long time.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33002
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33008
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33009
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 2 33004
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33005
Name     The Valley Road — Southern Approach~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The road north from Dreshdae enters the approach to the Valley of the
Dark Lords. The cliff faces begin to rise on either side, their red
stone carved with the tombs of the ancient Sith. Even on the road the
dark side presence is palpable — a pressure against the mind that
increases with every step north. The settlement lies to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33003
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33010
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 2 33005
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33006
Name     Dreshdae Cantina~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Dreshdae cantina is the only establishment on Korriban that could
be described as social. It achieves this distinction by maintaining
an unspoken rule that violence stays outside. The staff enforce this
with the particular authority of those who know exactly how much
the clientele needs this one neutral space. The drinks are strong,
the lighting is poor, and the conversations are not meant to be
overheard.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33003
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 2 33006
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33007
Name     Dreshdae Supply Depot~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A supply depot stocking the basics required by the Academy and its
students — ration packs, equipment components, medical supplies, and
the various tools needed to survive on Korriban. The prices reflect
the planet's remoteness and the captive nature of the market. The
operator conducts business with the weary efficiency of someone who
has been doing it a long time and has no expectations of improvement.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33003
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 1 33007
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33008
Name     The Northern Wastes — Western~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The northern wastes stretch away from the road in every direction,
their red stone broken by ancient impact craters and the occasional
collapsed structure that predates even the Sith. The wind is stronger
here, carrying the sound of something that is not quite howling. The
sky is clear but the light feels filtered through something that
does not scatter it quite correctly.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33004
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33011
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33009
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 3 33008
Reset M 0 33004 2 33008
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33009
Name     The Northern Wastes — Eastern~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The eastern reaches of the northern wastes are marked by a field of
ancient weapon impacts — craters of varying sizes suggesting a battle
fought here in the distant past. Fragments of armour and weapons
still protrude from the ground, too corroded to identify but clearly
old beyond reckoning. The dark side saturates the site.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33008
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33010
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33004
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 3 33009
Reset M 0 33003 2 33009
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33010
Name     The Valley of the Dark Lords — Entrance~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The entrance to the Valley of the Dark Lords is marked by two massive
carved pillars of dark stone, each bearing the faces of ancient Sith
Lords in high relief. The valley cuts between sheer red cliffs ahead,
its floor worn smooth by millennia of passage. The dark side energy
here is overwhelming — not just a pressure but a presence, as though
the valley itself is aware of arrivals and is forming opinions about
them. This is the resting place of the greatest Sith who ever lived.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33005
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33009
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33012
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33007 2 33010
Reset M 0 33003 1 33010
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33011
Name     The Northern Wastes — Deep~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The deep northern wastes are among the most inhospitable terrain on
a planet not renowned for hospitality. Rocky outcroppings provide
the only cover and the wind here has an edge that suggests the
planet itself is trying to remove unwanted visitors. The dark side
is present even here, far from the tombs — Korriban has been
saturated for so long it has nowhere left to go.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33008
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33012
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 3 33011
Reset M 0 33004 2 33011
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33012
Name     The Valley of the Dark Lords — The Long Walk~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The valley floor stretches north between its cliff walls, the tombs
of the ancient Sith carved into both faces. Names that shaped the
history of the galaxy — Marka Ragnos, Naga Sadow, Tulak Hord,
Ajunta Pall — each have their entrances here. The stone of the
valley floor is worn smooth and stained dark by millennia of dark
side energy seeping from the tombs. Walking this path is walking
through the concentrated history of the Sith Order.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33010
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33015
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33013
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33014
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33011
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33007 2 33012
Reset M 0 33003 1 33012
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33013
Name     The Tomb of Ajunta Pall — Entrance~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The entrance to the tomb of Ajunta Pall, the first Dark Lord of the
Sith, is cut directly into the cliff face. The doorway is framed
by carvings depicting his conquest and his fall — a Jedi who turned
to the dark side and in doing so created the Sith as a tradition.
The carvings are remarkably detailed and have been maintained by
the dark side energy itself. A long corridor descends into darkness.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33012
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33016
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33007 2 33013
Reset M 0 33003 1 33013
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33014
Name     The Tomb of Marka Ragnos — Entrance~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The grandest tomb entrance in the valley, befitting Marka Ragnos who
ruled the Sith Empire for a century and died only of age — a feat no
other Dark Lord has matched. The entrance is twice the height of any
other and the carvings are of extraordinary quality. His name above
the door is carved in letters a metre tall. Inside, the corridor
descends into the cliff with the confidence of something built to
outlast civilisation.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33012
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33017
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33007 2 33014
Reset M 0 33003 1 33014
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33015
Name     The Valley of the Dark Lords — Deep~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The deepest accessible section of the valley floor. The cliff faces
here are almost vertical and the sky above is reduced to a narrow
strip of burnt orange. The tombs in this section belong to the most
ancient Sith and their dark side presence is the most intense in the
valley. The air is noticeably cooler here despite the planet's heat.
Breathing takes slightly more effort. Concentration takes considerably
more.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33012
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33018
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33019
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33020
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33007 2 33015
Reset M 0 33000 2 33015
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33016
Name     The Tomb of Ajunta Pall — Antechamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The antechamber of Ajunta Pall's tomb is a broad vaulted space whose
walls depict the story of the Hundred Year Darkness — the war that
drove the first Sith from the Republic and created the Sith Empire.
The perspective of the carvings is clearly that of the defeated
exiles and the bitterness in the imagery is still palpable thousands
of years later. Three corridors lead deeper into the tomb.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33013
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33021
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33022
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33003 2 33016
Reset M 0 33007 1 33016
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33017
Name     The Tomb of Marka Ragnos — Antechamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The antechamber of Marka Ragnos's tomb is proportioned for a ruler —
vast, high-ceilinged, and decorated with the accumulated tribute of
a century of absolute power. Relief sculptures of conquered worlds
and subjugated peoples line the walls. The tomb has been sealed
for so long that the air has taken on a quality that is not quite
breathable and not quite not breathable.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33014
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33023
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33024
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33003 2 33017
Reset M 0 33007 2 33017
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33018
Name     The Tomb of Tulak Hord — Entrance~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The entrance to the tomb of Tulak Hord carries a different energy
than the others in the valley — more aggressive, more immediate.
Where other tombs feel ancient and patient, this one feels like
something coiled and ready. The doorframe is carved with dueling
figures — thousands of them, all ending the same way — and the
floor of the entrance corridor is darker than the stone around
it, stained by something that time has not removed.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33015
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33025
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33007 2 33018
Reset M 0 33003 1 33018
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33019
Name     The Tomb of Naga Sadow — Entrance~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The tomb of Naga Sadow is cut deeper into the cliff than any other
in the valley, as though the Dark Lord wanted maximum distance from
the surface. The entrance corridor slopes downward at a steep angle
and the air that rises from below is noticeably colder than the
valley outside. The carvings here depict space battles — the great
hyperspace war that Naga Sadow fought and lost — with extraordinary
astronomical accuracy.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33015
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33026
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33007 2 33019
Reset M 0 33003 1 33019
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33020
Name     The Valley — The Ancient Obelisk~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     At the northernmost accessible point of the valley floor stands a
single black obelisk of unknown origin. It predates the Sith, the
Republic, and every record that exists. Its surface carries markings
that no scholar has ever translated and its presence in the Force
is unlike anything else on a planet not short of unusual Force
phenomena. The dark side energy of the entire valley seems to
converge on this point.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33015
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33000 3 33020
Reset M 0 33007 2 33020
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33021
Name     The Tomb of Ajunta Pall — Inner Corridor~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A long corridor running deep into the cliff, its walls carved with
scenes from the life of the first Dark Lord. The corridor is cold
and the sound of footsteps echoes in a way that suggests the space
is larger than it appears. Tuk'ata markings on the floor indicate
these creatures consider the corridor their territory. The
antechamber lies to the south and the burial hall is ahead.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33016
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33027
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33003 1 33021
Reset M 0 33004 2 33021
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33022
Name     The Tomb of Ajunta Pall — Side Passage~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A side passage off the antechamber leads to a chamber that was clearly
used for rituals rather than interment. The floor is carved with
complex geometric patterns and the walls show scenes of Force
manipulation in techniques that are no longer practised. Sith relics
may still be found here by those willing to deal with the current
occupants.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33016
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33007 2 33022
Reset O 0 33005 1 33022
Reset O 0 33007 1 33022
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33023
Name     The Tomb of Marka Ragnos — Inner Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The inner hall of Marka Ragnos's tomb is proportioned on the same
scale as his antechamber — designed to remind visitors that he was
the most powerful Sith of his era. Trophy cases line the walls,
their contents long since removed by tomb raiders over the centuries,
though the cases themselves are sealed with wards that destroyed
those who opened them without the appropriate knowledge.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33017
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33028
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33007 2 33023
Reset M 0 33000 1 33023
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33024
Name     The Tomb of Marka Ragnos — The Records Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A chamber containing the official record of Marka Ragnos's reign —
not a celebration but an account, maintained with the precision of
absolute power comfortable enough in itself not to need flattery.
The records cover a century of Sith history in extraordinary detail.
The chamber connects to the antechamber.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33017
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33003 1 33024
Reset O 0 33005 1 33024
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33025
Name     The Tomb of Tulak Hord — Combat Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The primary hall of Tulak Hord's tomb is unlike any other in the
valley — it is not a burial space, it is a combat arena. A circular
fighting space occupies the centre of the hall, its floor worn smooth
and dark. The spirit of Tulak Hord himself challenges any who enter
this space worthy of his attention, and his definition of worthy
begins at an extraordinarily high bar.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33018
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33029
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33006 1 33025
Reset M 0 33007 2 33025
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33026
Name     The Tomb of Naga Sadow — The Deep Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The primary chamber of Naga Sadow's tomb is dominated by a massive
star map carved into the domed ceiling — a map of his hyperspace
war displayed with the perspective of someone who nearly won it.
The dark side presence here is enormous. Naga Sadow's spirit does
not simply haunt this tomb; it saturates it. The air tastes of
something ancient and the Force feels like walking into deep water.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33019
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33030
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33005 1 33026
Reset M 0 33007 2 33026
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33027
Name     The Tomb of Ajunta Pall — The Burial Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The burial hall of Ajunta Pall. His sarcophagus stands at the centre
of the room, still sealed, still warded with protections that have
functioned for millennia. The room is cold enough to see your breath
and the dark side presence is the most intense in the tomb. His spirit
is present here and aware. Being in this room is not unlike being
studied by something vast and interested.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33021
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33031
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33000 1 33027
Reset O 0 33000 1 33027
Reset O 0 33003 1 33027
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33028
Name     The Tomb of Marka Ragnos — The Sarcophagus Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The sarcophagus chamber of Marka Ragnos. His sarcophagus is enormous
and carved with scenes from every significant event of his reign in
miniature detail. The room is maintained by dark side energy that
has kept it in perfect condition since his interment. The presence
of Marka Ragnos himself is not spectral here but structural — he
is part of the room the way a foundation is part of a building.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33023
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33000 1 33028
Reset O 0 33000 1 33028
Reset O 0 33002 1 33028
Reset O 0 33006 1 33028
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33029
Name     The Tomb of Tulak Hord — The Sarcophagus Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     Tulak Hord's sarcophagus is smaller than expected for one of his
reputation — he had no interest in displaying power through scale.
What surrounds it instead are weapons, hundreds of them, all taken
from opponents he defeated in single combat over his career. The
collection represents some of the most skilled fighters who ever
lived, all of whom lost to Tulak Hord. The spirit here is
aggressive, watchful, and never fully at rest.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33025
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33006 1 33029
Reset O 0 33001 1 33029
Reset O 0 33004 1 33029
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33030
Name     The Tomb of Naga Sadow — The Weapon Vault~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A vault off the deep chamber containing the weapons and personal
effects of Naga Sadow. Unlike the main tomb the vault has been
raided, its contents partially removed over the centuries by those
bold or foolish enough to enter. What remains is still significant.
The spirit of Naga Sadow permits the vault to be viewed but
not without cost.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33026
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33005 1 33030
Reset O 0 33001 1 33030
Reset O 0 33003 1 33030
Reset O 0 33000 1 33030
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33031
Name     The Tomb of Ajunta Pall — The Secret Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A hidden chamber beyond the burial hall, not marked on any map that
has left Korriban. Ajunta Pall concealed his most personal and most
dangerous knowledge here — the techniques he developed during the
Hundred Year Darkness that the Republic found so threatening they
exiled an entire generation of Force users to prevent their spread.
The knowledge is still here. The question is whether you can take it.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33027
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33000 2 33031
Reset O 0 33000 1 33031
Reset O 0 33005 1 33031
Reset O 0 33007 1 33031
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33032
Name     The Sith Academy — Main Gate~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The main gate of the Korriban Sith Academy is built into the cliff face,
its archway carved with the history of the institution in compressed
relief. Above the gate the academy's motto is inscribed in ancient
Sith: Peace is a lie. There is only passion. The gate is open but
the acolytes flanking it make the implicit cost of entry clear.
The valley road is to the south and the academy grounds lie north.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33010
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33033
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 2 33032
Reset M 0 33002 1 33032
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33033
Name     The Sith Academy — Entrance Courtyard~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The entrance courtyard of the Sith Academy is a place of constant
evaluation. Acolytes train here under the observation of Overseers
who assess everything — strength, technique, aggression, intelligence,
and the particular quality the Sith value most: the willingness to
do whatever is necessary. Those who fail the assessment do not get
a second chance. The main gate is to the south and the academy
buildings lie ahead.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33032
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33034
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33035
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33036
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 4 33033
Reset M 0 33002 2 33033
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33034
Name     The Sith Academy — Main Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The main hall of the Sith Academy is a cathedral-scale space built to
impress upon arriving students the nature of what they are entering.
The Sith Code is inscribed above the entrance in letters that require
looking up to read — a deliberate design choice. Portraits of past
Headmasters and celebrated graduates line the walls. The current
Headmaster's portrait conspicuously has no name below it.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33033
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33037
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33038
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33039
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 3 33034
Reset M 0 33002 2 33034
Reset M 0 33008 1 33034
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33035
Name     The Sith Academy — Training Yard East~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The eastern training yard is used for combat training — bladed and
blaster disciplines both, with an emphasis on the former. The ground
is scarred from thousands of training sessions and the occasional
session that stopped being training partway through. The
Overseers who supervise training here do not intervene in
disputes between acolytes. Competition is the point.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33033
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 4 33035
Reset M 0 33002 1 33035
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33036
Name     The Sith Academy — Training Yard West~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The western training yard focuses on Force training — the application
of dark side power in practical situations. Targets of various kinds
are set up at intervals and acolytes practice Force techniques under
the cold observation of instructors who know exactly what they are
looking for and are not easily impressed. Exhaustion is not accepted
as an excuse to stop.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33033
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 4 33036
Reset M 0 33002 1 33036
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33037
Name     The Sith Academy — The Archive~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Sith Academy archive is a smaller and considerably more aggressive
collection than the Jedi Archives on Coruscant. Where the Jedi collect
broadly the Sith collect specifically — techniques, weapons research,
historical intelligence on enemies, and the accumulated knowledge of
every Sith who has contributed to the collection. Access is by merit
and merit is assessed by the archive master with a subjectivity that
serves as its own filter.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33034
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33040
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33002 1 33037
Reset O 0 33005 1 33037
Reset O 0 33000 1 33037
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33038
Name     The Sith Academy — The Proving Grounds~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Proving Grounds are where acolytes undergo their formal trials —
challenges set by the Overseers that test every quality the Sith
consider essential. The room is unremarkable in its appointments.
What happens in it is not. The record of each trial is carved into
the wall beside the entrance — name, date, and outcome. The list
of those who failed is significantly longer than the list of those
who succeeded.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33034
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33041
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33002 2 33038
Reset M 0 33001 2 33038
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33039
Name     The Sith Academy — The Headmaster's Office~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Headmaster's office is exactly what one would expect — austere,
functional, and arranged to give the occupant a comprehensive
positional advantage over anyone entering. The desk is large and
positioned with the wall behind it and clear sight lines to both
the door and the window. On it sits a single datapad, one personal
effect, and nothing else. The Headmaster values economy.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33034
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33008 1 33039
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33040
Name     The Sith Academy — Restricted Archive~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The restricted section of the Academy archive contains material that
even by Sith standards requires controlled access — techniques too
dangerous to teach in a classroom environment, intelligence too
sensitive for general circulation, and the personal records of Sith
Lords who made contributions they did not want widely attributed.
Access here is granted by the Headmaster directly and only to
those with a demonstrated need.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33037
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33008 1 33040
Reset O 0 33000 1 33040
Reset O 0 33005 1 33040
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33041
Name     The Sith Academy — The Dueling Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The dueling hall is the most used space in the Academy. Formal duels,
instructed sparring, and the informal violence that the Academy
permits between acolytes as a matter of policy all occur here.
The floor is dark stone that shows its history and the walls are
high enough to give aerial techniques room to develop. The Overseers
watch from elevated positions and their assessments of what they
observe carry significant consequences.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33038
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 4 33041
Reset M 0 33002 2 33041
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33042
Name     The Academy Dormitories — Entrance~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The entrance to the acolyte dormitories. If the rest of the Academy
is Spartan, the dormitories take that aesthetic to its logical extreme.
Bare stone, minimal lighting, and the constant awareness that the
person sleeping in the next bunk may consider you competition. Some
acolytes consider this the most challenging aspect of Academy life.
They are probably right.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33034
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33043
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 3 33042
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33043
Name     The Academy Dormitories — Main Block~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The main dormitory block houses the majority of the Academy's acolyte
population in rows of simple bunks. Personal possessions are limited
to what fits in a sealed container under the bunk. The social dynamics
here are complex, brutal, and educational in ways not covered by the
formal curriculum. Alliances form and dissolve quickly in this space.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33042
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 4 33043
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33044
Name     The Cave System — Upper Entrance~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A cave entrance in the cliff face below the Academy leads into an
extensive natural cave system that runs beneath the valley. The
Academy uses the upper sections for certain training exercises
that benefit from complete darkness and enclosed space. Beyond
the upper sections the caves become unmapped and increasingly
occupied by shyrack colonies. The academy grounds lie south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33033
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33045
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33004 3 33044
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33045
Name     The Cave System — Upper Passages~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The upper passages of the cave system are wide enough to move through
comfortably, though the floor is uneven and the ceiling height varies.
Bioluminescent organisms provide faint blue-green light at intervals.
The shyrack nesting areas begin further in and their sounds carry
through the rock. The entrance lies to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33044
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33046
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33047
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33004 4 33045
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33046
Name     The Cave System — The Shyrack Nest~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The primary shyrack nesting area. Hundreds of the creatures occupy
the ceiling of this large cavern, their collective sound a constant
shrill background noise. They react to light sources, sound, and
movement with immediate and coordinated aggression. The floor is
covered in generations of nesting material that makes footing
uncertain and the smell extraordinary. The passage out lies south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33045
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33048
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33004 6 33046
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33047
Name     The Cave System — The Crystal Vein~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A side passage that opens into a natural formation of dark crystals
running through the cave wall. These are not kyber crystals but
something related — dark-side saturated mineral formations that have
grown in the tomb valley environment over millennia. They glow very
faintly red in complete darkness and the Force presence around them
is cold and specific.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33045
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 33007 2 33047
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33048
Name     The Cave System — The Deep Cave~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The deepest accessible section of the cave system, a large natural
chamber where the dark side energy of Korriban's tombs has accumulated
over millennia. The shyrack presence here is at its most intense and
something else is also present — a dark side entity that has existed
in the cave since before the Sith built their tombs above. It is not
a spirit or a ghost. It is something that was here first.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33046
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33000 2 33048
Reset M 0 33004 4 33048
Reset O 0 33000 1 33048
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33049
Name     The Valley Outlook~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A natural plateau above the valley floor, accessible by a steep path
cut into the cliff face. From here the entire Valley of the Dark Lords
is visible — the tomb entrances carved into both cliff faces, the worn
valley floor below, the black obelisk at the northern end, and the
Academy built into the cliff to the east. The scale of what the Sith
built here over millennia is staggering from this vantage point.
~
#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    33015
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 2 33049
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33050
Name     The Wasteland — The Crash Site~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A ship came down here a very long time ago. The wreckage is barely
recognisable as having ever been a vessel — decades of Korriban's
environment have corroded and half-buried most of it. From the
fragments that remain visible it appears to have been a Republic
era cruiser, its markings long since scoured by red sand. What
brought it down and what happened to the crew are questions
with no living witnesses.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33008
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 2 33050
Reset O 0 33005 1 33050
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33051
Name     The Wasteland — The Ancient Battlefield~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     Beneath the red dust of this section of wasteland lies an ancient
battlefield where a significant engagement was fought in the era
of the Great Hyperspace War. Weapons, armour fragments, and the
occasional skeletal remain protrude from the ground after particularly
strong winds. The scale of what is buried here is visible only from
altitude. The dark side energy of thousands of violent deaths is
still present in the ground.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33009
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33052
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 3 33051
Reset M 0 33003 1 33051
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33052
Name     The Wasteland — Northern Reaches~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The northern reaches of the Korriban wastelands, as far from the
valley and the academy as it is practical to travel on foot and
still be able to return. The landscape here is unchanged from
its natural state — raw red rock and dust under a hot orange sky.
The dark side is present even here, ambient and deep, the
accumulated energy of thousands of years of Sith activity that
has saturated the planet itself.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33051
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33053
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 3 33052
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33053
Name     The Wasteland — The Bone Field~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A field of bones covers this section of wasteland — not a deliberate
arrangement but an accumulation. Things die here in numbers. The
bones are of many different species and many different eras. Some
are very old and some are recent. The tuk'ata use this area as a
hunting ground and the evidence of that is comprehensive.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33052
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33009
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33003 3 33053
Reset M 0 33009 3 33053
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33054
Name     The Wasteland — The Dark Side Vergence~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A point in the open wasteland where the dark side energy of Korriban
converges with unusual intensity — a vergence visible to Force
sensitives as a distortion in the air above the spot. The Sith have
known about this location for millennia and have used it for purposes
that are now only partially documented. Standing on it is an
experience that those who have survived it tend not to describe in
detail.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33052
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33004
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33000 2 33054
Reset O 0 33003 1 33054
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33055
Name     The Korriban Wastes — The Red Canyon~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A canyon of deep red stone cuts through the wasteland, its walls
rising twenty metres on each side. The floor is firm and the passage
through it provides some shelter from the constant hot wind. Sith
script is carved into the canyon walls at intervals — old enough
to predate the Academy, suggesting the canyon was known and used
long before the institution was built.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33008
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33056
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 2 33055
Reset M 0 33003 1 33055
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33056
Name     The Red Canyon — Southern End~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The southern end of the red canyon opens back onto the main wasteland.
A carved stone marker at the canyon mouth was once an important
navigational reference — the carved symbols indicate directions and
distances to locations now buried or destroyed. One direction marker
still legible points toward what the ancient inscription calls
the place of first binding.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33055
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33004
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 2 33056
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33057
Name     The Valley — The Tomb of an Unknown Lord~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A tomb entrance without a name above the door. The carvings that
once identified this Sith Lord have been deliberately removed —
not by time but by another hand. Whatever was done here to earn
that erasure from the record must have been extraordinary even by
Sith standards. The tomb itself is intact and the dark side presence
within is substantial. Whoever this was, they were powerful.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33015
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33058
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33007 2 33057
Reset M 0 33000 1 33057
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33058
Name     The Unknown Tomb — Inner Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The inner chamber of the nameless tomb is the most unsettling space
in the valley. The carvings here have also been removed but less
completely — fragments remain that suggest the kind of power this
Sith wielded and why it was considered necessary to remove their name
from history. The sarcophagus is intact. The spirit within it is aware
of your presence and has been waiting for someone worth speaking to.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33057
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33000 2 33058
Reset O 0 33000 1 33058
Reset O 0 33003 1 33058
Reset O 0 33005 1 33058
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33059
Name     The Academy — The Meditation Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A chamber within the Academy used for dark side meditation — the
drawing in of dark side power through focused emotional states.
Unlike Jedi meditation which seeks stillness, Sith meditation seeks
amplification. The Academy's meditation chamber is designed to
facilitate that — its construction channels the dark side energy
of the valley directly into the space.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33034
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33002 1 33059
Reset M 0 33001 2 33059
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33060
Name     The Academy — The Armoury~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Academy armoury maintains weapons for student use during training.
Everything here is functional and nothing is ornamental — the Sith
have no time for decorative weapons. The armoury also contains
confiscated items taken from those who arrived on Korriban with
equipment deemed too valuable to leave in their possession.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33034
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33002 1 33060
Reset O 0 33001 1 33060
Reset O 0 33004 1 33060
Reset O 0 33006 1 33060
#ENDROOM


#ROOM
Vnum     33061
Name     The Valley — The Sith Warrior Barracks (Ruins)~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The ruined remains of barracks that once housed the Sith warriors who
guarded the valley. The structures collapsed centuries ago but the
walls still stand to waist height in places. The dark side energy
that preserved the warriors themselves has not extended to their
living quarters. The ruins connect to the valley floor.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33012
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33007 3 33061
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33062
Name     The Valley — The Offering Pit~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A circular pit cut into the valley floor, its purpose documented
in the Academy archive as a site of ritual offering. The depth
is difficult to determine in the darkness below. Items dropped into
it do not make a sound on landing. The dark side energy around
the pit has a specific quality — acquisitive, attentive, hungry.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33012
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33000 2 33062
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33063
Name     The Tomb of Ajunta Pall — The Lower Passage~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A lower passage within the tomb, accessed through a concealed door
in the burial hall. The air here is notably colder than elsewhere
in the tomb and the dark side presence has a specific texture —
personal, watchful, old. The stone is carved with scenes from the
Jedi Order that Ajunta Pall left behind, rendered with the
ambivalence of someone who never entirely resolved his feelings
about his origins.
~
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    33027
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33000 1 33063
Reset O 0 33000 1 33063
Reset O 0 33007 1 33063
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33064
Name     The Valley — The Dark Side Spring~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A natural spring emerges from the cliff face here, its water dark
and still. The water is not toxic but it is not natural either —
it has absorbed too much dark side energy over too many centuries
to be classified as simply water. It is drunk by the tuk'ata
and no other living thing on Korriban. Sith alchemists have
studied it and found properties they declined to publish widely.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33015
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33003 2 33064
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33065
Name     The Academy — The Alchemy Laboratory~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A specialised laboratory within the Academy where Sith alchemy is
taught and practised. The equipment here handles materials that
require dark side energy to work with safely and the safety
protocols are enforced with the seriousness of those who have
seen what happens when they are not followed. The results
of successful alchemy work are among the most powerful items
on Korriban.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33037
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33002 1 33065
Reset O 0 33004 1 33065
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33066
Name     The Wasteland — The Standing Stones~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A circle of standing stones in the open wasteland, their arrangement
clearly deliberate and their age clearly immense. The stones are of
a type not found in the surrounding geology, suggesting they were
brought here from elsewhere. Each stone is carved on its inner face
with a single Sith rune. The circle produces a mild Force effect
when stood within — a slight enhancement of dark side connection
that is persistent while inside it.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33004
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33008
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33000 2 33066
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33067
Name     The Valley — The Sith Altar~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A massive stone altar stands in an alcove carved into the valley wall
between tomb entrances. The altar is not associated with any specific
Sith Lord — it predates all of them. Dark stains on the stone's surface
and in the channels carved around its base tell a history of use that
stretches back further than the written Sith record. The dark side
around it is thick and specific.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33015
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33000 2 33067
Reset M 0 33007 1 33067
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33068
Name     The Academy — The War Room~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A strategic planning room within the Academy where military doctrine
and tactical planning are taught. Holographic maps cover the walls
and a central table displays a tactical assessment of the current
political and military situation in the galaxy. The Sith view
strategic knowledge as inseparable from personal power.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33034
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33002 1 33068
Reset M 0 33008 1 33068
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33069
Name     The Tomb of Marka Ragnos — The Throne Room~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     Marka Ragnos had a throne room built within his tomb where his spirit
could hold court. The throne of dark stone is intact and his spirit
does occasionally choose to occupy it. Being in the presence of the
spirit of the most successful ruler the Sith Empire ever produced
requires considerable preparation.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33028
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33000 1 33069
Reset O 0 33002 1 33069
Reset O 0 33006 1 33069
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33070
Name     The Academy — The Indoctrination Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The first room every new acolyte is brought to upon arrival. The
indoctrination delivered here establishes the fundamental framework
of Sith philosophy that everything subsequent builds on. The room
is designed to be disorienting — unusual geometry, lighting that
creates false shadows, and acoustics that make the instructor's
voice seem to come from everywhere simultaneously.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33033
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33002 1 33070
Reset M 0 33001 2 33070
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33071
Name     The Valley — Between the Tombs~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A narrow passage between two tomb entrances in the valley wall,
too small to be a designated route but worn smooth by use. The tomb
walls on each side are close enough to touch simultaneously. The dark
side energy of two great Sith Lords presses in from both sides and
the combined effect in this narrow space is significant.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33015
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33012
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33007 2 33071
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33072
Name     The Wasteland — The Toxic Flats~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A flat expanse of pale ground where chemical runoff from ancient
Sith experiments has created a terrain hostile to most organic life.
The ground is crusted and unstable in places and the fumes that rise
from cracks in the surface are best not breathed for extended periods.
The Korriban hounds avoid this area, which says something.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33004
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33052
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 1 33072
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33073
Name     The Academy — The Punishment Block~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The Academy calls it the correction block. It is where acolytes who
have demonstrated insufficient progress or obedience are sent. The
environment is designed to be educational through discomfort. Very
few acolytes are sent here twice and the ones that are tend to be
notably more capable than their peers afterward.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33043
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33002 1 33073
Reset M 0 33001 1 33073
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33074
Name     The Cave System — The Bone Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A large natural chamber where generations of shyrack activity have
accumulated an extraordinary quantity of remains. The floor is
covered in bones to a depth that makes movement difficult and the
shyrack presence above is constant. Dark side entities from the
deeper cave are also attracted to this chamber and their influence
is palpable here.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33046
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33004 5 33074
Reset M 0 33000 1 33074
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33075
Name     The Valley — The Meditation Alcoves~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A row of small alcoves carved into the valley wall between the major
tomb entrances, sized for a single individual. These were used by
Sith who came to the valley to draw on its dark side energy for
meditation and power. The dark side energy in each alcove is focused
and intense.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33015
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 2 33075
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33076
Name     The Academy — The Research Wing~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A wing of the Academy dedicated to active research — the development
of new dark side techniques, the study of Force phenomena, and the
ongoing refinement of Sith alchemy. The research conducted here has
contributed significantly to the Academy's reputation and its graduates
are among the most innovative Force users in the galaxy.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33037
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33002 1 33076
Reset O 0 33005 1 33076
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33077
Name     The Wasteland — The Sith Marker Trail~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A series of carved stone markers leads across the wasteland on a
route the current maps no longer show. The markers are ancient Sith
and the inscriptions give directions in a dialect requiring specialist
knowledge to translate. Following the trail leads toward something
that the maps have forgotten, which on Korriban is either significant
or simply a place that killed everyone who went there.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33054
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33056
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 2 33077
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33078
Name     The Valley — The Tomb Robber's Camp~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The remains of a camp set up by tomb robbers seeking the artefacts
of the ancient Sith. They clearly had some success before their work
came to an abrupt end — tools, containers, and partially filled packs
are scattered around the site. The details of what ended the operation
are not recoverable from what remains, which is itself informative.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33012
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 33005 1 33078
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33079
Name     The Academy — The Outer Wall Walk~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The walkway along the top of the Academy's outer wall, used for
perimeter patrol and for the panoramic view it provides of the valley
and wastelands. From here the entirety of the Valley of the Dark Lords
is visible. Academy guards patrol this walk with the alertness of
personal survival instinct rather than institutional expectation.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33033
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 2 33079
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33080
Name     The Valley — The Hall of Waiting~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A long hall carved into the valley wall between the major tombs, once
used by those awaiting audience with a Sith Lord's spirit. The practice
of petitioning tomb-bound spirits was common in the old Empire. The
hall has not been used for that purpose in centuries but the waiting
quality of the space remains.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33015
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33012
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33007 2 33080
Reset M 0 33000 1 33080
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33081
Name     The Wasteland — The Western Reaches~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The western edge of the Korriban wasteland where the flat terrain
breaks into a series of low rocky ridges. The ridges provide reasonable
concealment and have been used for that purpose by beings on Korriban
for very different reasons over the centuries.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33008
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33082
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 3 33081
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33082
Name     The Wasteland — The Western Reaches Deep~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     Deep in the western reaches the rocky ridges become higher and the
passages between them narrower. The dark side is present but thinner
than in the valley — here it feels more like weather than presence.
It is as close to a neutral space as Korriban offers.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33081
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 2 33082
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33083
Name     The Cave System — The Collapsed Passage~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A passage in the cave system that has partially collapsed, reducing
the available width to a gap that requires careful movement to navigate.
Beyond the collapse the cave continues and the sounds from deeper suggest
significant shyrack activity. The collapse looks recent by cave
standards — within the last century or two — and something caused it
that was not geological.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33045
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33046
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33004 3 33083
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33084
Name     The Academy — The Senior Acolyte Quarters~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Senior acolytes — those who have survived long enough to be considered
for elevation — are housed in slightly less Spartan conditions than
their juniors. Individual rooms rather than open dormitories. The
improvement is modest by any external standard and significant by
Academy standards.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33043
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 3 33084
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33085
Name     The Valley — The Eastern Path~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A path along the eastern cliff face of the valley giving access to
tomb entrances set higher in the cliff. The path is narrow in places
and the drop to the valley floor below is significant. The tombs
accessible from this path are among the oldest in the valley and
some have not been entered in recorded history.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33012
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33086
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33007 2 33085
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33086
Name     The Valley — The Upper Tomb Tier~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The upper tier of tombs in the eastern cliff face, their entrances
smaller and less grand than those below but their dark side presence
no less significant. These are the tombs of Sith whose names have
been lost to time. What they contain has not been catalogued.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33085
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33000 2 33086
Reset M 0 33007 2 33086
Reset O 0 33005 1 33086
Reset O 0 33007 1 33086
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33087
Name     The Academy — The Trophy Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A hall displaying items taken from defeated enemies over the
institution's history. The collection begins with items from the
Great Hyperspace War and continues to the present day. The display
philosophy is Sith — these are demonstrations of capability, not
celebrations of history.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33034
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 33000 1 33087
Reset O 0 33005 1 33087
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33088
Name     The Valley — The Bone Road~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A section of the valley floor where the dark side has preserved the
remains of those who entered the valley and did not leave, arranging
them in a line that parallels the main path. Whether this arrangement
is deliberate or an incidental product of the dark side energy is a
question the Academy teaches acolytes to stop asking.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33015
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33012
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33007 2 33088
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33089
Name     The Cave System — The Echo Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A natural chamber with extraordinary acoustic properties — sounds made
here are amplified and returned in sequences that do not match the
geometry of the space. The Sith have used this property for specific
rituals involving sound as a medium for dark side power.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33047
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33004 2 33089
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33090
Name     The Wasteland — The Impact Crater~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A large impact crater in the wasteland, its origin unclear. Too large
for a meteorite, too precisely circular for geology. The Academy archive
contains a single notation: source unknown, date unknown, avoid. The
dark side energy at the crater's centre is stronger than anywhere else
in the wasteland outside the valley.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33054
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33000 2 33090
Reset M 0 33009 2 33090
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33091
Name     The Valley — The Inscription Wall~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A flat section of valley wall used as a writing surface by Sith over
thousands of years. The inscriptions overlap in layers that a
specialist could read as a chronological history of everyone who
passed through the valley and felt moved to leave a record of it.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33012
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33001 1 33091
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33092
Name     The Academy — The Comms Room~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Academy's communications room handles contact with Sith operatives
across the galaxy, coordinates with other Sith institutions, and
monitors Republic and other communications of intelligence value.
What passes through this room shapes what the Sith do next in ways
that are rarely visible until afterward.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    33039
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33002 1 33092
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33093
Name     The Valley — The Dark Side Pool~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A natural pool of dark liquid in a chamber carved into the valley wall,
accessible only through a narrow entrance. The dark side energy
concentrated in the liquid is the most intense in the valley outside
the individual tombs. Sith who have used it for ritual purposes
describe the experience as definitive. Very few of them describe it twice.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    33015
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33000 2 33093
Reset O 0 33003 1 33093
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33094
Name     The Wasteland — The Sith Outpost (Ruins)~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The ruins of a Sith outpost that once served as a waystation between
the valley and the spaceport. The walls are down to foundation level
and most contents are unidentifiable. The foundations are Sith-worked
stone, still solid, still resonant with a residual energy that has
not dispersed in centuries.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33004
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33002
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33009 2 33094
Reset O 0 33005 1 33094
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33095
Name     The Academy — The Garden of Thorns~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The Academy has a garden. It grows plants used in alchemy and ritual,
several of which are hazardous to handle without appropriate knowledge.
The plants are cultivated with the same precision applied to everything
else at the Academy and the Overseer responsible is regarded with a
specific wariness by their colleagues.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33033
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33002 1 33095
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33096
Name     The Valley — The Ritual Circle~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A circle of dark stone set into the valley floor, its surface covered
in carved runes of power and binding. This circle has been in continuous
ritual use for longer than any other site in the valley outside the
tombs. The dark side energy accumulated through use is staggering —
standing within it requires considerable Force sensitivity to survive
comfortably.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    33020
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    33015
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33000 3 33096
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33097
Name     The Academy — The Observation Tower~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A tower above the Academy main building giving a comprehensive view
of the valley, the wastelands, and the spaceport approach. Used for
security observation, astronomical study relevant to Sith ritual
timing, and watching what happens in the valley below — which on
any given day includes things worth monitoring.
~
#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    33034
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 33002 1 33097
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     33098
Name     The Korriban Wastes — The Southern Flats~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The flat southern reaches of the Korriban wastelands, between the
spaceport road and the more broken terrain further out. The dark side
is present at its lowest ambient level here — a background condition
rather than a force.
~
